drm/amdgpu: don't load the secure display TA on the Surface Laptop 4 (AMD)

psp_v12_0 keeps the secure display TA on for every Renoir, and at each
boot this laptop's PSP refuses it:

  amdgpu 0000:03:00.0: RAP: optional rap ta ucode is not available
  amdgpu 0000:03:00.0: psp gfx command LOAD_TA(0x1) failed and response
  status is (0x7)

The refused TA is SECUREDISPLAY 0x27000008, the newest linux-firmware
carries; HDCP and DTM load. amdgpu already gives up on it after the
refusal, and its only user is the display's region CRC, a debugfs test
feature. Skip it on this model, by its GPU's subsystem ID 1414:0051, so
the boot says the TA isn't available rather than reporting a failure.
psp_v10_0 does the same for Raven with this TA version.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/psp_v12_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/psp_v12_0.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/psp_v12_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/psp_v12_0.c
@@ -63,6 +63,11 @@ static int psp_v12_0_init_microcode(struct psp_context *psp)
 	if (!(adev->apu_flags & AMD_APU_IS_RENOIR))
 		adev->psp.securedisplay_context.context.bin_desc.size_bytes = 0;
 
+	/* The Surface Laptop 4 (AMD)'s PSP refuses the TA with status 0x7. */
+	if (adev->pdev->subsystem_vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_MICROSOFT &&
+	    adev->pdev->subsystem_device == 0x0051)
+		adev->psp.securedisplay_context.context.bin_desc.size_bytes = 0;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
